Title: What They Called Recovery
Credit: Animated feature screenplay — source-developed working scene
Author: Christopher Kokkinos
Draft date: 2026-10-10
Status: Independent screenplay development under DEC-0019; refinements during production

INT. RUTH'S OFFICE / VARIOUS - LATER THAT WEEK

Ruth gives Zoe a limited update, not a list she must memorise.

Cain is charged first over Jackie detention, movement and interference with safeguarding. Mac is charged later over placement records, conspiracy and financial arrangements; he continues to cooperate. Voss and Vale remain under investigation. Their accounts establish their actions too.

These are charges and inquiries, not convictions or a solved archive.

Westmere confirms some restricted cases legitimate. Others need work. North Vale checks further references. No final total appears.

INT. RUTH'S OFFICE - ANOTHER AFTERNOON

Helen and Brian remain in their house. Zoe watches rain on the window.

ZOE
My room?

RUTH
As far as I know, still there. They've written separately. Asked whether you might consider contact. They'll accept no.

Zoe remembers a badly repaired cabinet, school mornings, Helen untangling hair. Those memories stand alongside the glass.

ZOE
Not yet. Don't destroy the letters.

Three days later she asks for Helen first page only. Reads a handwritten admission: she knew enough to refuse; loss and grief explain her, not a right to choose for Zoe or her original family.

Zoe folds the page.

ZOE
Enough.

Ruth takes it back. Brian envelope remains unopened.

INT. TEMPORARY ACCOMMODATION - DAYS LATER

The location and practical rules were explained through Ruth and current safeguarding. Nothing claims permanence. Elias has a separate room down the corridor.

He returns from a doctor and tells Zoe himself. Rib pain, previous physical dependence and fear of repeating it discussed. The pain plan changed. No miraculous recovery.

Zoe does not count his tablets or become his monitor. He takes prescribed treatment without making refusal a test of strength.

INT. RUTH'S OFFICE - TWO WEEKS AFTER THE ARTICLE

RUTH
What name do you want used?

ZOE
Mine.

RUTH
Which one?

The earlier name is in the sealed folder. Zoe does not need to erase either history to choose today.

ZOE
Use Zoe. Keep the other one private until I decide otherwise.

Ruth explains records may eventually require correction; not everything must be settled now. Writes Zoe wishes, not an adult substitute.

INT. TEMPORARY ACCOMMODATION - LATER

Jackie calls about her new school: assigned resilience, refused, received coastal erosion instead. Zoe laughs until she has to call back.

Her own tutor has left algebra on the table. Surviving a conspiracy has not improved it.

The news article moves off the front page. The investigations do not stop. Zoe puts the phone down and returns to one difficult equation, with a future not reducible to the archive.
